@algekalipso @bayeslord as best as i can introspect, prediction error when mentally evaluating propositional statements is implemented as simultaneous activation of mutually-incompatible branches of evaluation and the sense of dissonance between them. this might also be described as crossed 'lines of attention', perhaps.

intermediary steps within the evaluation process are implemented by subtle neuromuscular latches/'tanha', sometimes layered on top of one another in a kind of stack machine. these in and of themselves can be kind of unpleasant.

but mental evaluation of propositional statements is a recent innovation in our evolutionary history – a "CPU on a GPU" – and could well be a local minima stumbled into by accident. i wonder if there could be another way.id: 1597179922086125568
created_at: 2022-11-28T10:45:42Z
